/* book Worked example 2: Q: A formed channel has a 60 mm web and two 25 mm flanges, all 1.5 mm thick, in the same alloy (E = 72 GPa, ν = 0.33, σcy = 300 MPa). Find the local buckling stresses of the web and flanges and the crippling load by Needham's method.
   1. Web, both edges supported (k = 4): σel = 4 × 66,455 × (1.5/60)² = 166.1 MPa. Flange, one free edge (k = 0.425): σel = 0.425 × 66,455 × (1.5/25)² = 101.7 MPa. The flanges buckle first.
   2. Cut the web at mid-depth: two angles, each with a 25 mm flange (free edge) and a 30 mm half-web (cut edge, held by the other half). One edge free, so Ce = 0.342.
   3. b′ = (25 + 30)/2 = 27.5 mm, b′/t = 18.33, (b′/t)0.75 = 8.860.
   4. σcs = 0.342 × 4,647.6/8.860 = 179.4 MPa, below σcy.
   5. Area: each angle (25 + 30) × 1.5 = 82.5 mm², the section 165 mm².
   6. Pcs = 179.4 × 165 = 29,601 N = 29.6 kN.
   Answer: σel = 166.1 MPa (web) and 101.7 MPa (flanges); σcs = 179 MPa and Pcs = 29.6 kN. */
